meta {
  name: 01-Register
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/api/auth/register
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "amaka.okafor.lekki+{{run_tag}}@gmail.com",
    "password": "MyLekkiFlats2025!",
    "fullName": "Amaka Okafor",
    "displayName": "Amaka O.",
    "phone": "+2348031234567",
    "role": "OWNER",
    "publicRole": true
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 202
}

script:post-response {
  // Stash the email so I can log in with it next.
  bru.setVar("amakaEmail", "amaka.okafor.lekki+" + bru.getEnvVar("run_tag") + "@gmail.com");
  bru.setVar("amakaPassword", "MyLekkiFlats2025!");
}

docs {
  # Day 1, ~9:30pm — just got home from Abuja office.

  My friend Funke told me about DreamHomes at lunch. Sitting on the bed
  scrolling on my phone. Let me just see what this is about.

  I'm picking OWNER because I'm the landlord, not an applicant. I added my
  Glo number too — that's the one I use for everything property.

  Spec promised 202 with no body. I expected to also get a token back so I
  could use the app right away — instead I have to make a SECOND call to
  log in. That's annoying for a tired person. Why would you make me type
  my password twice?
}
